python311.zip
.
..\site-packages
..\..
..\..\override

# site-packages is listed here rather than passed via PYTHONPATH:
# an embeddable Python with a _pth file is isolated and silently ignores
# PYTHONPATH. `import site` is deliberately absent - this site-packages
# has no .pth files, so site processing has nothing to do.
#
# The last two entries exist for the same reason and one more. Isolated mode
# also leaves the script's own directory off sys.path: sys.path[0] is this
# zip, and the `.` above means the interpreter's directory, not the caller's.
# Without them a script could only reach its own siblings by calling
# sys.path.insert first - and that is a statement, so every import after it
# trips E402. The plugin market's verify workflow runs ruff with
# --ignore-noqa, which leaves no way to silence E402, so the paths belong
# here rather than in the scripts.
